<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04UT">Remark <span data-tag="04UT">10.2.1.31</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}_{/X} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{1}_{/X} \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{/X}$ be sieves on an object $X$. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{0}_{/X}$ is dense, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}^{1}_{/X}$ is also dense. See Proposition <a data-tag="0312" href="/tag/0312">7.3.8.12</a>. </p>
